<title>USA: Audiovox Corp Q3 August 31 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Audiovox Corp Q3 August 31 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>HAUPPAGE, N.Y. 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In Thousands, Except Share and Per Share Data)</p>
<p>							    Three Months</p>
<p>							   1996	 1995</p>
<p> Net sales					 $142,828     112,177</p>
<p> Net income (loss)				    767     (6,385)</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per common share	    0.08	(0.71)</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding (primary)   9,285,188   9,038,742</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding (diluted)   9,325,588   9,038,742</p>
<p> Pro forma net loss per common share	     --   (0.36)(A)</p>
<p>							    Nine Months</p>
<p> Net sales					 $406,515    $349,378</p>
<p> Net income (loss)				  1,394     (9,621)</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per common share	    0.15	(1.06)</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding (primary)   9,285,188   9,038,742</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding (diluted)   9,330,217   9,038,742</p>
<p> Pro forma net loss per common share	     --   (0.39)(B)</p>
<p>(A)  Proforma adjustments have been made to reflect results before the $7.8 million writedown of inventory, $4.0 million for closing retail outlets and the $8.4 million gain on the sale of CellStar shares, net of income tax.</p>
<p>(B)  Proforma adjustments have been made to reflect results before the $2.9 million expense related to the issuance of warrants, the $7.8 million writedown of inventory, $4.0 million for closing retail outlets and the $8.4 million gain on the sale of CellStar shares, net of income tax.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
